invariant: INV-16
file: aead.c
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: aead_open_cpu checks its tag under WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever the
  session's ch_cfg.cpu states, so every record and packet a session opens
  runs Poly1305 on the decomposition, and the bit picks nothing there.
  The verdicts are the same. bin/widemul_runtime_test requires the entry
  to call the native copies alone under a value with
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY.

--- old
    if (!tag_matches(widemul_of_cpu(cpu), key, nonce, aad, aad_len, ct, n, tag)) {
--- new
    if (!tag_matches(WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED, key, nonce, aad, aad_len, ct, n, tag)) {
